{"c":[{"id":"4593d0105bc0e4e0","sum":"B21-B23: planRequest names a window one way; only hello host: true is a host; revokes are immediate; presses only SAFE_PRESSES; --act-pids needs FIXTURE_ACTS; undo marks; reader wants a 0700 socket dir and helperAuth (launch.ts); swift mutation runs use --build-path /tmp.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"66b7d7e70abf08e9","sum":"B21-22: planRequest window by {pid,number,title} or windowId; posted keys skip an inactive app's key equivalents; a consumer connection is a host session (evals call hostConnected); grant revoked on pause/stop; mutation runs: swift test --build-path /tmp.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"2f09076641c97656","sum":"B21: planRequest names a window by {pid,number,title} or windowId, never both (unread = unseenWindow); rebuild caret-screen after mutated swift tests; posted keys skip an inactive app's key equivalents; Return in a frontmost one-line field presses the default button, unreported.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"09ccc8ad4b5ca18a","sum":"planRequest names its window by {pid, number, title} or windowId, never both; unread = unseenWindow, neither = ScreenModel.userWindow (v2/host planError needs an unseenWindow sentence). swift test on mutated source rebuilds .build/debug/caret-screen: rebuild before GUI evals.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T015937Z-41933c0bb214864e","text":"planRequest names its window as window {pid, number, title} or windowId, never both; an unread one is unseenWindow; neither means the frontmost app's last focused window (ScreenModel.userWindow). v2/host's planError switch needs an unseenWindow sentence (B21).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T015937Z-53ebaedecebf757b","text":"swift test on a mutated source rebuilds .build/debug/caret-screen; rebuild from the restored source before any GUI eval runs those binaries (B21 caught it by timestamp).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f69cdfcee30c7eb9","sum":"B21: keys posted to an inactive app's pid skip AppKit key equivalents (posted Return never ran the default button, Space pressed a focused one); frontmost, Return in a single-line field presses the default button, which the reader does not report.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T015937Z-ebf44f31f7890c91","text":"A key posted to a pid whose app is not active skips AppKit key equivalents: the fixture's default button never ran on posted Return or Enter (0 of 10), Space pressed a focused button 5 of 5. The reader places key presses from cached focus and default button (B21).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T031707Z-b7d2054c5f965771","text":"AppKit presses a window's default button on Return typed into a single-line text field: frontmost fixture, Note focused, Send ran 5 of 5. B21's reader counts no Return while a text field has focus (brief), so that submit goes unreported (gui/keys-front).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"9b3d66084a009c9f","sum":"B22: a consumer connection is a host session (tasks revoked on close; evals call helper.hostConnected); pause/stop/settings/disconnect revoke the act grant at once, Helper.authorize before each act; mutation runs use swift test --build-path /tmp, grep 'recorded an issue'.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"dc5a5754f076b1b1","sum":"B22: each consumer connection is a host session; tasks bind to it and are revoked when it closes; in-process evals must call helper.hostConnected(id). Pause, stop, settings and disconnect revoke the act grant at once; Helper.authorize is asked before each act.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T150809Z-35454632bb9daf62","text":"B22: each consumer connection is a host session; accepted tasks bind to the one that started them and are revoked when it closes; runs with no Tab need a connected host. In-process tests and evals that play the host must call helper.hostConnected(id) or no skill runs on its own.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T150824Z-0b7169f06df102c4","text":"B22: every pause, take over, stop, Caret pause, settings/permission/skill/memory change and host disconnect revokes the act grant at once (Executor.revoke/recheck); the executor also asks Helper.authorize right before each write, press, raise and calendar add.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ccdfe7e5f11e70bf","sum":"B22: a consumer connection is a host session (tasks revoked when it closes; evals call helper.hostConnected). Mutation runs: swift test --build-path /tmp/... keeps .build/debug clean; Swift Testing prints 'recorded an issue' for a failure, grep that.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T150829Z-581618fb20568b53","text":"B22: each consumer connection is a host session; accepted tasks bind to the session that started them and are revoked when it closes; runs with no Tab need a connected host. In-process tests and evals that play the host must call helper.hostConnected(id).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T150830Z-a3b40432646c1572","text":"B22: swift test --build-path /tmp/... keeps mutation runs out of .build/debug; Swift Testing marks failures 'recorded an issue', not ✘, so grep that when checking a mutation was caught.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b90f59e8e9d017fa","sum":"B22-B23: --act-pids needs CARET_SCREEN_FIXTURE_ACTS; presses only SAFE_PRESSES; only a hello with host: true is the host; undo marks give notSameElement; reader needs a 0700 socket dir and helperAuth first (launch.ts, --auth-fd); crash eval SIGKILLs a helper mid run.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"e0ee3433a46919d2","sum":"B22-D2-03: --act-pids needs CARET_SCREEN_FIXTURE_ACTS=fixture-only; presses only whole SAFE_PRESSES labels (risk.ts, RiskTable, press-risk.json together). Open-time event card is needsYou; only a hello with host: true is the host (evals: hostConnected).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"8d97b0b1c518449c","sum":"B22: --act-pids needs CARET_SCREEN_FIXTURE_ACTS=fixture-only; window ids are opaque to the helper. Presses only whole SAFE_PRESSES labels, never in a system prompt; change risk.ts, RiskTable.safePresses and press-risk.json together.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T150830Z-cd56cc67608f9643","text":"B22: --act-pids now needs CARET_SCREEN_FIXTURE_ACTS=fixture-only and caret-fixture pids; window ids are <pid>-<start µs>-<generation>-<n>, opaque to the helper.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T150843Z-b8f6b3671dd764ee","text":"B22: presses only whole labels in risk.ts SAFE_PRESSES / RiskTable.safePresses, never in a system prompt (subrole AXSystemDialog or AXSystemFloatingWindow, or a TCC/SecurityAgent process); change both lists and press-risk.json together.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e926b62b147229c0","sum":"D2-03: an open-time event card is needsYou with choices; a closed-line Tab re-offers it under a new key. B23: only a consumer hello with host: true is the host (v2/host must send it or no skill runs alone); in-process evals call helper.hostConnected(id).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T153943Z-e96b8d822d84ddbb","text":"D2-03: an event card whose time is open (no AM/PM, no end) is figure needsYou with a choices block; the host's closed-line Tab sends no variants row, so the helper adds nothing and re-offers the card under a new key (offerWithdrawn reoffered).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T171742Z-0e49751b5685c975","text":"B23: only a consumer hello with host: true counts as the host; other consumers bind their own work but keep no run with no Tab alive. v2/host must send host: true, or no skill runs on its own. In-process evals still call helper.hostConnected(id).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c7edb83e11969db2","sum":"B23: undo sends sameAs with a mark (reader: notSameElement otherwise; fakes test/fake-marks.ts); crash-recovery-eval SIGKILLs a helper mid run. Reader needs a 0700 socket dir; caret-screen needs --auth-fd and helperAuth first (launch.ts; evals --auth-fd 0).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"200602a89c015e6e","sum":"B23: undo sends sameAs with a mark; the reader answers notSameElement unless the element is the one it wrote (fakes: test/fake-marks.ts). crash-recovery-eval.ts SIGKILLs a real helper mid skill run; its 'helper still running' check catches crashes after the last publish.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T171742Z-101e1e3d273eec2a","text":"B23: forward value writes carry a mark and undo sends sameAs; the reader answers notSameElement unless the element at the key is the one it wrote (per app worker, gone on reader restart). Test fakes use test/fake-marks.ts; marks.replace(windowId, key) plays a replaced field.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T171742Z-362dd90f069eee83","text":"B23: scripts/crash-recovery-eval.ts SIGKILLs a real helper child mid skill run while the script plays reader and host; its 'restarted helper is still running' check is what catches a crash after the last publish (an id collision did exactly that).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"cf937cd80d01ef87","sum":"B23: the reader connects only to a 0700 socket dir of the user's own (tests: mkdtemp). caret-screen needs --auth-fd (32-byte secret) and trusts a helper whose first line is helperAuth (HMAC challenge+pid); use launch.ts; evals pass --auth-fd 0 and sendSecret.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T171742Z-7971f1eeb5bd9db9","text":"B23: the reader connects only to a socket whose directory is 0700 and the user's own (never /tmp itself; HelperServer chmods its dir). Tests and evals put sockets in mkdtemp directories.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T171817Z-c0fbce2e0a5b8f78","text":"B23: caret-screen needs --auth-fd (32-byte secret) and trusts only a helper whose first line is helperAuth (HMAC of challenge+pid, pid = LOCAL_PEERPID). Use helper/src/launch.ts; evals pass --auth-fd 0, sendSecret(reader, s), new HelperServer(..., s).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"861d3a8ad4100669","sum":"B23-W3: connectNative port keeps the MV3 worker alive; accept.ts needs CARET_HEAVY_LOCK_HELD=1 under a held lock and --sign-identity; caret-screen needs --auth-fd 0; person fill asks whose then values; Chrome AX shows a select's chosen option only.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"0a68eb7c3188c374","sum":"B23/W1/W2/I1: recovery rows return stopped with undo; open connectNative port keeps the MV3 worker alive; accept.ts under a held lock needs CARET_HEAVY_LOCK_HELD=1; worker result() forwards only named ActAnswer fields; caret-screen needs --auth-fd 0 + secret.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"842e4a5a9e2cd880","sum":"B23/W1/W2: recovery.sqlite rows of runs under way return stopped with undo; react-select's chosen input has opacity 0 (walker waives it); an open connectNative port keeps the MV3 worker alive; under a held heavy lock accept.ts needs CARET_HEAVY_LOCK_HELD=1.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"685d64f7872e343d","sum":"B23/W2: recovery.sqlite holds sealed rows of runs under way; at start their skills go back on Tab, rows list as stopped with undo, id generators skip ids in use. react-select sets its input opacity 0 once chosen; walker.visibleReactSelect waives opacity there.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T171834Z-0d54f9ef314f8bad","text":"B23: recovery.sqlite holds sealed rows of runs under way (skill_id in clear). At start each row's skill goes back on Tab; readable rows list as 'Stopped when Caret restarted, at step N of M' with undo. Id generators skip ids in use (idTaken).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T181245Z-06db563b8bbd4ad9","text":"W2: react-select makes its input opacity 0 whenever a value is chosen, so the walker's opacity rule dropped it; walker.visibleReactSelect waives only opacity inside a visible react-select box.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"224bf2f9191d9b3d","sum":"W1/W2: open connectNative port keeps the MV3 worker alive (360 s, CfT 154); headless CfT registers with LaunchServices, so caret-screen --only-pids reads it. accept.ts: page acceptance; under a held heavy lock set CARET_HEAVY_LOCK_HELD=1 or its bridge build deadlocks.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T181245Z-2154a79bf4058057","text":"W2: headless Chrome for Testing registers with LaunchServices, so caret-screen --only-pids <pid> reads it; accept.ts uses that for the AXManualAccessibility log check (Electron fixture via helper/scripts/electron-setup.sh).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T181245Z-2950b78a7b855fe8","text":"W1: an open connectNative port kept the MV3 worker alive through 360 s idle (same instance, CfT 154). Page acceptance: node fixtures/web-form/accept.ts; under a held heavy lock set CARET_HEAVY_LOCK_HELD=1 or its bridge build deadlocks.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7f5511b9b77cbeaa","sum":"W1/W2/I1: CfT reads NM manifests only from <user-data-dir>/NativeMessagingHosts; worker result() forwards only named ActAnswer fields; page.sock key is HMAC(secret,'caret-page-key'); caret-screen needs --auth-fd 0 + secret; golden lines are indexed 0-based on both sides.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"bc66b962416e3ac5","sum":"W1/W2: CfT 154 with --user-data-dir reads NM manifests only from <user-data-dir>/NativeMessagingHosts; headless Chrome takes one command-line URL; the worker's result() forwards only named ActAnswer fields, so a new one (choice, attached, pageChanged) goes there.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T181245Z-9a5093647c9001cd","text":"W1: Chrome for Testing 154 with --user-data-dir reads Native Messaging manifests only from <user-data-dir>/NativeMessagingHosts; headless Chrome refuses more than one command-line URL; chrome.runtime.getFrameId is undefined in content scripts.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T181245Z-d139eff429d072a1","text":"W2: the worker's result() forwards only named fields of ActAnswer; a new field (choice, attached) must be added there or it silently never reaches the helper.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"8a8589948371a0f4","sum":"I1: page.sock key is HMAC(launch secret,'caret-page-key'); bridge needs engineWelcome.pid == LOCAL_PEERPID; caret-screen needs --auth-fd 0 + 32-byte secret on stdin. Golden protocol.ndjson lines 60-68 are indexed 0-based in protocol.test.ts and GoldenTests.swift.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T183627Z-67627518ce143f34","text":"I1: page.sock's key is HMAC(launch secret, 'caret-page-key') in <sock>.key, and the bridge requires engineWelcome.pid == LOCAL_PEERPID; main.ts starts no page.sock without --auth-fd. Since B23, anything that spawns caret-screen must pass --auth-fd 0 and a 32-byte secret on stdin.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T183627Z-707cb99ebedd3d58","text":"I1 golden order: protocol.ndjson lines 60-66 are B23's (hello/helperAuth/marks), 67-68 W2's pageEngine; tests index them 0-based in protocol.test.ts and GoldenTests.swift.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"95a52729c4179521","sum":"B24/I2: person fill asks whose, then values (4 Jev calls); space Groq writer calls 30 s; Chrome AX shows a select as AXPopUpButton, chosen option only. W3: Helium reads NativeMessagingHosts in a temp profile; accept.ts needs --sign-identity, boots a launchd testhost.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"a993ea246e3968f1","sum":"B24/I2: a person's fill asks whose, then values (4 Jev calls, PER_FILL); space Groq writer calls 30 s; TextEdit opens CLI files only from its container tmp; Chrome AX shows a select as AXPopUpButton with only its chosen option; toWindowSnapshot mirrors Chrome AX.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d32f644355f794d8","sum":"B24: a fill asks whose first, then values: 4 Jev calls (tests use PER_FILL); space Groq writer calls 30 s; sandboxed TextEdit opens a command-line file only from ~/Library/Containers/com.apple.TextEdit/Data/tmp.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T192504Z-05aef102d22989aa","text":"B24: fill asks in two stages when a field takes a person's details (whose first, then values), so a fill is 4 Jev calls, not 2; tests that count calls use PER_FILL. Groq's qwen3.8 hits 429 token limits within ~20 plans; space writer calls 30 s.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T192504Z-2947a2d88b908a7e","text":"B24: TextEdit is sandboxed: a file named on its command line opens only from inside ~/Library/Containers/com.apple.TextEdit/Data/tmp (realfill-capture.ts makes its own folder there and deletes it).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"712d8e92089c7858","sum":"B24/I2: Chrome AX shows a native select as AXPopUpButton holding only its chosen option, so fill hands selects off; page-link toWindowSnapshot mirrors Chrome AX (AXTimeField; radios in an AXGroup per name; options as AXMenuItem).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T192504Z-d09a0e8b1bd722e1","text":"B24: Chrome's AX shows a native <select> as AXPopUpButton whose only child is the selected option; the option list is not readable without opening it, so fill names selects as hand-offs with no value (capture-2 probe).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T195842Z-c30fb40a821e024f","text":"I2: page-link.ts toWindowSnapshot must match Chrome AX for fill/controls.ts: time is AXTimeField, radios sit under an AXGroup per name attribute, select options are AXMenuItem children. PageControl has no fieldset legend, so page radio groups have no label.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0581e9c7aa2f84db","sum":"W3: Helium 0.18 loads --load-extension on a temp profile, reads NativeMessagingHosts there; page.sock proofs bind the helper pid. Bridge reaches host over XPC; accept.ts needs --sign-identity/--other-identity, boots a temp launchd testhost. Headless CfT: createTarget steals focus","tree":{"c":[{"id":"13ae7e710e2343cf","sum":"W3: Helium 0.18 loads --load-extension on a temp profile and reads NativeMessagingHosts there; page.sock proofs bind the helper pid so a swapped socket can't relay the host's hello.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T204321Z-5a96910dba2d6b69","text":"W3: Helium 0.18 loads --load-extension on a temp --user-data-dir and reads Native Messaging manifests from <user-data-dir>/NativeMessagingHosts (accept.ts --browser passes 42/42); its Web Store page offers Add to Helium.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T204321Z-74ab7d13fad22cf2","text":"W3: page.sock proofs both bind the helper pid (bridgeProof too), or a same-user process that swaps the socket path can pass the host's hello to the real helper and keep that session.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"94d9cdb89929ed3f","sum":"W3: bridge reaches host over XPC (no page.sock key); accept.ts needs --sign-identity/--other-identity, boots a temp launchd testhost. Headless CfT: createTarget steals focus, activateTarget won't return it.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T204321Z-903b513efe20fc90","text":"W3: caret-bridge reaches the Caret host over XPC (CaretBridgeXPC), never page.sock; no <sock>.key exists. accept.ts needs --sign-identity <team SHA-1> (and --other-identity for refusal checks) and runs caret-bridge-testhost as a temporary launchd job it boots out.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T204321Z-98052ff285eab267","text":"W3: headless Chrome for Testing gives focus to a window CDP Target.createTarget opens and Target.activateTarget does not move it back; chrome.windows focused is reported in headless. Page window focus = active tab of the focused, last-focused window.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
